For a new file:
git add "file"
Make changes to file, then:
git status % To see what changes are ready to be committed
git commit -m "comment"
git push -u origin main % To update remote repository (Github)
For a new edit:
git add "file" for all files changed, and then follows steps for the making a new file process
To make a new directory, place a file in it, and then git add "file" for that file
To grab a file from a remote repository, use: git pull % look up arguments


